In his response video, captioned &#8220;Ffs,&#8221; Levy said in part, &#8220;Women wearing short shorts at the gym does not make them whores; it makes the men calling them whores misogynists.&#8221;

His comments section was flooded with support, including from a handful of music stars. Jewel thanked Levy, while Wicked star Kristin Chenoweth posted a &#8220;100&#8221; emoji and Lisa Loeb commented alongside a fire emoji &#8220;Thank you.&#8221;

Maggie Baird, the activist mother of Billie Eilish and FINNEAS, shared Levy&#8217;s video to her Instagram Story with her own lengthy caption. &#8220;Thank you [Dan Levy]!&#8221; she started. &#8220;I literally gasped when [Shane Gillis] said this on [ SNL ]. I felt it physically (and was reminded of the horrible Bill Burr monologue),&#8221; she added, referencing Burr&#8217;s controversial 2020 appearance on the sketch comedy show, when he complained that white women had hijacked the &#8220;woke&#8221; movement and that Pride Month shouldn&#8217;t be so long. Baird continued: &#8220;I come from the sketch comedy world and am not squeamish around comedy, but how can men and comedy writers still think this is funny! It’s actually dangerous for women to promote this bullsh&#8211;.&#8221;

Flavor Flav also platformed Levy&#8217;s video, sharing an article about his response on X with the message: &#8220;Important allyship.&#8221;

